# LaTeX build artifacts and scratch renders. The volume is built in the catalogue, not
# here, so these should never appear; the rules are kept because a clone used for
# proofreading is the obvious place somebody runs pdflatex once.
build/
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz

# No assembled volume and no PDF is ever published. Only the Markdown chapters and their
# figures are. These are blanket rules rather than named files, so a new output name
# cannot slip through: the whole volume, a single chapter, or anything else.
*.pdf
*.html

# Named explicitly as well, so the intent survives anyone relaxing the rules above.
ZeroKnowledge_Embedded_Top20_v2.pdf
ZeroKnowledge_Embedded_Top20_v2.html
ZeroKnowledge_Embedded_Supplement.pdf
ZeroKnowledge_Embedded_Supplement.html
project-*.pdf
project-*.html
chapter-*.pdf
chapter-*.html

# --- The authoring half, which is not published ---------------------------
#
# What this repository publishes is Markdown: one chapter under chapters/, the companion
# under docs/, and the figures as rendered SVG. The LaTeX those are generated FROM stays
# in the catalogue on the authoring machine. A reader needs neither a TeX installation
# nor a second copy of every chapter in a second markup language to read the book.
#
# The loop is, in the catalogue volume:
#     python mdbuild.py --out build/md
#     python publish.py
# and publish.py writes chapters/, docs/, figures/ and CONTENTS.md here.
# Nothing else writes them.
#
# No LaTeX of any kind is published, figure sources included. One blanket rule rather
# than a list of paths, because a list is something a new file can be added outside of:
# this cannot be got round by putting a .tex somewhere new.
*.tex

# Every rule here is anchored with a leading slash so it matches only at the repository
# root. Without the anchor, "figures/" would also ignore a figures directory published
# inside some future project folder.
/sections/
/build.py
/mdbuild.py
/publish.py
/prepublish.py
/lint.py
/palette.tex

# Local virtual environments and editor state
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Journals and correspondence never reach a published repository, private shares
# included. The working record of this volume, with its pivots and its learnings, is
# kept minute by minute in the catalogue, which is local only and is never pushed. A
# published repository carries the work, never the running record of doing it.
private_journal/
correspondence/
DIARY*.md
# Referee reports and the editor's consolidation, added Friday 6 November 2026.
# A review is a working record of the same kind: it names what was wrong before it
# was right, and it is for the author rather than for the reader.
review/
referee_*.md
editor_*.md

# The scratch file a hand-over writes a commit message into, because PowerShell has no
# usable heredoc and git commit -F is the way in. The commit carries it; the tree does not.
commit-message.txt

# Lean build artifacts, from the development published under lean/
.lake/
lean/.lake/
lean/build/
*.olean
*.ilean
*.trace
